Design for Hazardous Material Isolation in the context of remanufacturing is a strategy that focuses on designing products to safely and effectively isolate hazardous materials. This approach is crucial for ensuring that during the remanufacturing process, these materials are contained and do not pose risks to workers or the environment. By integrating DfHMI, products are designed in a way that hazardous components are easily identifiable and separable, facilitating their safe handling and disposal. This not only enhances the safety and efficiency of the remanufacturing process but also aligns with environmental and health regulations, contributing to sustainable remanufacturing practices.